+/* Pending clears
+ *
+ * zink submits a pending glClear as its own render pass whenever the app
+ * switches framebuffer before drawing: an empty pass that clears and stores a
+ * whole attachment, and later a pass on the same image that loads it back and
+ * overwrites it. Each pass costs kernel jobs and a full tile store, and the
+ * load re-reads what the empty pass just wrote.
+ *
+ * A dynamic render pass that only clears (loadOp CLEAR, storeOp STORE, render
+ * area equal to the whole view, no draws) is not submitted. Its attachments are
+ * kept as pending clears instead. A later pass that attaches the same image
+ * view over the same area takes the clear as its own load op (a LOAD becomes a
+ * CLEAR); every other access submits the clears first, at that point of the
+ * command stream: a pass that attaches the image in any other way, a
+ * non-graphics sub-command, a barrier that names the image or makes attachment
+ * writes visible, ExecuteCommands and EndCommandBuffer. Draws and state
+ * commands need no hook: reading the cleared image any other way needs one of
+ * those first.
